Payap is built on the emerging open banking landscape in New Zealand. The core challenge was turning a technically complex, heavily constrained payment method into something that felt simple, smooth, and trustworthy. As the product evolved, wider business needs, including merchant growth, pushed the experience in a more social direction, opening up new ways to drive engagement and give people value beyond the payment itself.

The result humanises a technically complex system. By designing around the constraints of open banking and layering in stronger engagement mechanics, Payap became more than a way to pay: a product that makes payments easier, more rewarding, and part of everyday life.
